   Just camp out as the altar (or beside it) and wait for monsters until
   they start coming. you've been to minetown, sufficient monsters will
   come. Patience. If you have a blindfold and telepathy, use it to see
   whether any have generated and move up or down the screen so they can
   get to the room with the altar if they're having problems. They
   always know where you are, they just can't always figure out how to
   get to you. 

   I frequently get 3 or 4 artifacts by donating at an altar on the
   first or second level before I've even been to sokoban. You'll get
   more food too from drops and corpses as you get weak. Only eat after
   you get weak and that way satiation won't be a problem - *never* eat
   while satiated. If you don't know why, you can read the rot13 below
   or I'll repost with a longer message. Suffice it to say that it
   *would* not help your situation. 

   A *lot* of people seem to forget (well I do myself sometimes) that
   the levels regenerate monsters if you stay there long enough, and it
   isn't 2000 turns even, you'll get new monsters appearing after
   800-1200 turns, just enough for a food ration. 



